    "result_text": "Green. The change is complete and the full suite passes.\n\n## What I did\n\nReleased version 2 of the owner identity while keeping structural impact low \u2014 each edited function stays simple and I avoided touching the large REST controller entirely.\n\n**Version-2 identifiers** (one-line hash-input change each; every identifier now differs from v1 and no v1 value can recur, since the uppercase `\"V2\"` tag is unreachable by the lowercased/E.164-normalized v1 inputs):\n- `MemberIds.build` \u2014 mixes the `V2` tag **and** the region into the hashed portion (`HASH8`). The visible `REGION` prefix stays the plain region, so `locality`, `timezone` and the owner segment (all read back via `regionOf`) remain plain `NSW`.\n- `Households.id` \u2014 SHA-256 input prefixed with `V2`.\n- `IdentityKeys.of` \u2014 SHA-256 input prefixed with `V2`.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):\n- Added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema and nested `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` under a top-level `identity` object; removed the three from the top level.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`.\n- The mapper maps into `identity.*`, adds `apiVersion`, and ignores top-level `householdId`.\n\n**Audit event** (contained entirely in `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 the controller call site is unchanged):\n- Added `schemaVersion: 2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the v2 identity's region + membership level, both emitted in `toJson()`.\n\n**Compile fix:** `OwnerWelcomeNotificationAdvice` read the now-moved `OwnerDto.getMemberId()`; repointed it to `getIdentity().getMemberId()` with a null guard.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The audit line now reads e.g. `{\"schemaVersion\":2,...,\"customerCode\":\"NSW26DD5C34099\",\"membershipLevel\":2,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, and the acceptance test (`apiVersion` = 2, nested `identity.*` present, top-level identifiers absent) passes.",
