    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The handler is the **v1** controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, mapped via `@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` + `/owners`), which takes a `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`. Because the work is spread across a servlet filter, security, request-body advices, Bean Validation, MapStruct mapping, entity setters, the service, and response-body advices, the order below follows the actual request pipeline.\n\n## 1. Servlet filter \u2014 idempotency (runs first, before Spring MVC)\n`OwnerIdempotencyFilter` (`@Order(HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)`):\n- Only when an `Idempotency-Key` header is present on a POST to `\u2026/api/owners`.\n- If the key was seen before \u2192 replays the cached response body with **HTTP 200**, controller never runs.\n- Otherwise, if the controller ultimately returns 201, caches the response bytes under that key (in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap`, process-local).\n\n## 2. Security\n- Method-level `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold **OWNER_ADMIN**.\n\n## 3. `beforeBodyRead` request-body advice (raw JSON, before binding)\n- **`OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice.beforeBodyRead`** \u2014 parses the raw JSON and **injects a computed `householdId`** into the body: `Households.id` = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(\"V2\" + normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)`.\n\n## 4. `afterBodyRead` request-body advices (bound DTO, before controller) \u2014 each can reject\nThese run before Bean Validation. In effect:\n- **`OwnerRequiredFieldsAdvice`** \u2192 **400** if any of firstName, lastName, city, telephone are missing/blank (whitespace counts as blank); address is satisfied by either `address` or `addressLine1`.\n- **`OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice`** \u2192 **400** if the email domain is exactly mailinator.com, tempmail.com, or guerrillamail.com.\n- **`OwnerRegistrationDateAdvice`** \u2192 **400** if a supplied `registrationDate` is after today.\n- **`OwnerPostcodeAdvice`** \u2192 **400** if a 4-digit postcode is outside its city's region band (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099).\n- **`OwnerTelephoneLengthAdvice`** \u2192 **400** if the E.164-normalized national number has the wrong length (`+61`\u21929 digits, `+1`\u219210).\n- **`OwnerDailyLimitAdvice`** \u2192 **429** if \u2265 100 owners already have today's (business-day) registration date. (Loads all owners.)\n- **`OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`** \u2192 **409** if \u2265 50 existing owners are in the same city (trim + lowercase).\n- **`OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice.afterBodyRead`** \u2192 **409** if an existing non-deleted owner has the same `identityKey` = `SHA-256hex(\"V2\" + telephoneE164 + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName))`.\n\n(These advices share the same `@Order`, so their relative order among themselves is not strictly deterministic \u2014 but each is an independent gate as listed.)\n\n## 5. Bean Validation (`@Valid` on the DTO)\nField constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/'/-).\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`).\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`.\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`, `@Pattern` requiring **exactly 10 digits** (any formatting).\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`.\n- `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)` each (nullable).\n- `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`.\n- `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (nullable). `title`, `householdId` \u2014 unconstrained.\n\n(No `@InitBinder` and no custom `ConstraintValidator` exist.)\n\n## 6. Mapping DTO \u2192 Owner entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 normalizations\n- `telephone` \u2192 E.164 via `TelephoneNormalizer` (assumes `+61`, drops leading `0` if no `+`).\n- `registrationDate` \u2192 supplied date or today, then rolled forward to a business day (`BusinessDays`, skips weekends + fixed 2026 holidays).\n- `address` \u2192 `AddressNormalizer.compose(addressLine1, addressLine2, address)`.\n- Entity setters re-normalize on assignment: telephone \u2192 E.164, address \u2192 normalized, **email \u2192 lower-cased**.\n- Entity-level constraints also apply: `telephone` must match `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`; firstName/lastName/address/city `@NotEmpty`.\n\n## 7. Service \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` (`@Transactional`)\nFor a new owner, loads **all** existing owners once, then in order:\n1. **`assignMemberId`** \u2014 builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region from city/postcode, 2-digit fiscal year, 8 hex of `SHA-256(\"V2\"+region+telephone+lastName)`, Luhn check digit), de-duplicated against existing member ids by appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026.\n2. **`assignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` (same first+last, case-insensitive); then `householdMemberCount` (same `householdId`, incl. self); then freezes **`membershipLevel`** = household-capped level (`MembershipLevels.cap`, at most one above the household's max).\n3. **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to an existing non-deleted owner with same postcode + same `soundex(lastName)` but a different identityKey (else null).\n4. **`ownerRepository.save`** \u2192 `em.persist` (new) into table `owners` (pets cascade `ALL`). No `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callbacks.\n\n## 8. Back in the controller \u2014 audit side-effects\n- Emits two lines on the **`AUDIT`** logger: a formatted line (id/memberId/registrationDate/membershipLevel) and a JSON line from `OwnerCreatedEvent.next(...)` (record with a static `AtomicInteger` sequence stamping a monotonic `seq`, plus derived `ownerSegment`). This is a **log line, not a Spring `ApplicationEvent`**.\n- Builds the response DTO (`toOwnerDto`) with many derived read-only fields (displayName, initials, identity block, fiscalYear, membershipPoints/level, locality, segment, timezone, contactPreference, ageBand, telephoneDisplay, selfLink).\n- Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n## 9. `ResponseBodyAdvice` chain \u2014 mutates the outgoing DTO\n- **`OwnerWelcomeNotificationAdvice`** \u2014 emits a `NOTIFY` log line (\"welcome owner\u2026\"). No real email is sent.\n- **`OwnerRiskFlagAdvice`** \u2014 sets `riskFlag` = possibleDuplicate OR disposable-adjacent email (subdomain of a disposable domain) OR city count \u2265 40.\n- **`OwnerCapacityWarningAdvice`** \u2014 sets `capacityWarning` = city count in [40, 49].\n- **`OwnerBulkSignupAdvice`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = owners-created-today > 80.\n\n(These three each re-query all owners to count.)\n\n---\n\n**Worth flagging:** there is no password encoding (owners have no password), no `ApplicationEventPublisher`/Spring events, and no actual email \u2014 the \"event\"/\"notification\"/\"audit\" are all just log lines on the `AUDIT`/`NOTIFY` loggers. Also note the DTO's `telephone` pattern demands exactly 10 digits while the entity requires E.164 `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` and a separate advice enforces per-country national-number lengths \u2014 three overlapping phone rules. A v2 controller exists but is mapped elsewhere; the `POST /api/owners` endpoint is the v1 one described here."
